    "q-142896": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142896",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.25$ | $0$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=9$ | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(0<X\\le 6\\,|\\,Y=3)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
      "worked_solution": "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X\\le 6\\,|\\,Y=3) & =\\frac{P((0<X\\le 6),Y=3)}{P(Y=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=3,Y=3)+P(X=6,Y=3)}{P(Y=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3,3)+f(6,3)}{{f}_{Y}(3)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(3) & =f(0,3)+f(3,3)+f(6,3)+f(9,3) \\\\  & =0+0.1+0+0.1 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(3,3)=0.1$ and $f(6,3)=0.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X\\le 6\\,|\\,Y=3) & =\\frac{f(3,3)+f(6,3)}{{f}_{Y}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1+0}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
