    "q-142943": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142943",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
      "worked_solution": "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=3)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=y\\,|\\,X=3)=\\frac{P(X=3,Y=y)}{P(X=3)}=\\frac{f(3,y)}{{f}_{X}(3)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.55$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $y\\in {1,2,3},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=1\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{f(3,1)}{{f}_{X}(3)}=\\frac{0.4}{0.6}=\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ P(Y=2\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{f(3,2)}{{f}_{X}(3)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.6}=\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(Y=3\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{f(3,3)}{{f}_{X}(3)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.6}=\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
